3334 0 obj
  << /ActualText (We initially explored the dataset\047s native geometry using K\055Means\054 K\055Medoids\054 Hierarchical Clustering and DBSCAN in the principal components space\056\n\nContinous Geometry\072 PCA space lacks natural boundaries\056 K\055Means optimization shows no \042elbow\042\054 and DBSCAN fails by merging almost all data into a single cluster\054 revealing dense\054 overlapping multi\055morbidities rather than distinct clusters\056 \nNo Confounding Bias\072 Adjusted Rand Index \050ARI\051 metrics are coherent with a clustering driven by ECG morphology\054 not demographics \050age\054 sex\054 weight\051\056\nUnsupervised Limits\072 Label Powerset \050LBS\051 suggests that clinical co\055morbidities act as continuous topological \042bridges\042\054 preventing clean geometric separation\056\nPC Interpretation\072 Despite the overlap\054 some structural anomalies subclasses \050CLBBB\057CRBBB\051 separate cleanly along PC 2 \050ventricular depolarization vector\051\054 achieving high Enrichment Factors \050EF \076 30\051\056\050\nWithout natural geometric partitions\054 supervised architectures are necessary to explicitly force diagnostic boundaries\056 \050Our empirical benchmarking established a clear performance hierarchy across tabular learning architectures\072\050)
     /K [ 14 ]
     /P 3335 0 R
     /Pg 3306 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

