3364 0 obj
  << /ActualText (From the Shapley values of our best\055performing model\054 XGBoost\054 we can further demonstrate the robustness and clinical relevance of our analysis\056 Indeed\054 there is a strong correspondence between the importance assigned by the Shapley values to specific features and the medical knowledge underlying each diagnostic superclass\072\nConduction disturbances \050CD\051\072 relevance of PR interval and the QRS complex\056\nMyocardial infarction \050MI\051 and ST\057T changes \050STTC\051\072 closely related from a clinical perspective\054 as both are associated with ischemic damage\054 main features related to ST\055segment and T\055wave morphology\054 also Q\055wave for MI\056\nHypertrophy \050HYP\051\072 again ST\055segment abnormalities relevant\054 but also QRS complex amplitudes\056)
     /K [ 29 ]
     /P 3365 0 R
     /Pg 3306 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

