3382 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Our results suggest that statistical learning achieves a performance competitive with DL models on raw signals\054 while retaining a critical advantage\072 clinical interpretability\056  Shapley values confirmed strong alignment between feature importance and medical knowledge\054 with PR interval and QRS complex driving CD\054 ST\055segment and T\055wave governing MI and STTC\054 and QRS amplitudes central to HYP detection\056  Among multi\055label strategies\054 probabilistic chains outperformed Binary Relevance\054 while greedy approaches suffered from error propagation\056 Functional Data Analysis further enriched the framework via MFPCA morphological components\054 and TreeSHAP\057mRMR reduced the feature space by 75\045 with negligible performance loss \024 advocating for interpretable\054 lightweight statistical models as a robust alternative to black\055box architectures in clinical decision support\056)
     /K [ 38 ]
     /P 3383 0 R
     /Pg 3306 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

